{"name":"Monza","hex":"#c7031e","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Monza","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A city and comune, the capital of Monza and Brianza province, Lombardy, Italy, best known for its Grand Prix circuit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Monza"}],"entries":[{"title":"Monza","blocks":[{"text":"Monza is a city and comune (municipality) in the region of Lombardy in northern Italy. Situated on the Lambro river about 15 kilometres (9.3 mi) north-northeast of Milan, it is the capital of the Province of Monza and Brianza and the largest city in the Brianza area, forming a part of the Milan metropolitan area. With a population of 123,672, it is the third-largest city in Lombardy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Reggia_di_Monza.jpg/330px-Reggia_di_Monza.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monza","wikidata":"Q6252"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Monza_Duomo_di_San_Giovanni_Battista_Esterno_Facciata_Frontone_1.jpg/500px-Monza_Duomo_di_San_Giovanni_Battista_Esterno_Facciata_Frontone_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Monza_Duomo_di_San_Giovanni_Battista_Esterno_Facciata_Frontone_1.jpg/1280px-Monza_Duomo_di_San_Giovanni_Battista_Esterno_Facciata_Frontone_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Monza_Duomo_di_San_Giovanni_Battista_Esterno_Facciata_Frontone_1.jpg/500px-Monza_Duomo_di_San_Giovanni_Battista_Esterno_Facciata_Frontone_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMonza_Duomo_di_San_Giovanni_Battista_Esterno_Facciata_Frontone_1.jpg"},{"srcset":"http